
Approach: Linear Traversal

Initialize count = 0.

Iterate through each student using an index i.

Check whether queryTime is greater than or equal to startTime[i] and less than or equal to endTime[i].

If both conditions are true, increment count.

Return count.

The interval is inclusive, so students starting or finishing exactly at queryTime are counted.




















class Solution {
    public int busyStudent(int[] startTime, int[] endTime, int queryTime) {
        int count = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < startTime.length; i++) {
            if (startTime[i] <= queryTime && queryTime <= endTime[i]) {
                count++;
            }
        }

        return count;
    }
}
